tip: | Look at the barrel. | A round thing still follows the grid: its rim is an ellipse twice as wide as it is tall, the same 2:1 as a tile.
tip: 3 | Shade in bands. | A curved side has no single face, so the light falls in vertical bands. Lightest a third of the way in from the left, a step per band, darkest on the right.
tip: 4 | Hoops curve with the rim. | A straight hoop would flatten the barrel. These dip in the middle, like the front of the rim, so the form stays round.
tip: | Try it. | Run Lighten / Darken down one band and see how little it takes to make the barrel shinier or duller. | shade
